{
  "proposal_id": "CP-73F2103E",
  "topic": "Replace Internal HTTP with Native IPC Layer",
  "category": "architecture",
  "description": "All internal module-to-module communication shall migrate from HTTP on port 8022 to native IPC. HTTP remains only for external clients and cross-machine federation. 1. Native IPC module registry (direct calls + ring buffer). 2. SPSC ring buffer for small payloads (<4KB, 9.9 ns). 3. Shared memory maps (mmap) for large payloads (>4KB, zero-copy). 4. HTTP endpoints preserved as thin wrappers for external access. 5. Benchmark: internal calls sub-100ns vs 1-10ms HTTP.",
  "proposer": "Architect",
